
;;
	a cast is written as:
	(type)

	it takes the value on top of the stack and reinterprets
	it as the given type
	the cast is only a change of interpretation, the bits are
	left alone

	casts are only available inside an ops block
	the type may be any primitive

	in an expression, a cast changes how the following
	operations see the value
	in a procedure body, a cast is used the same way, applied
	to whatever value is on top at that point
;;

main:(){
    0xFFFFFFFF bazz @4
    bazz!4 (u4) dmp
}

bazz:[s4]
foo:(u4:s4){ (s4) }